<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar outflows at $51 mln Oct 28.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar outflows at $51 mln Oct 28.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $51 million deficit on October 28 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank data supplied to banks.</p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the central bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON OCTOBER 28</p>
<p>Exports: $147.5 million</p>
<p>Imports: $202.1 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $182.2 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $178.6 million</p>
<p>Deficit: $51 million</p>
<p>OCTOBER DOLLAR FLOWS UP TO DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $3.198 billion</p>
<p>Imports: $3.528 billion</p>
<p>Financial buy: $5.686 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $3.757 billion</p>
<p>Net surplus: $1.599 billion</p>
<p>Note: the figures were rounded off.</p>
<p>-- Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroom, 55-11-2324411</p>
</text>
